<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Otho of Tournay</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">13th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otho">Otho</a> of Tournay was a knight of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade">Fourth Crusade</a> who received the barony of Kalavryta, one of the original twelve baronies of the Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaea">Achaea</a> in the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a>. The barony comprised twelve knight's fiefs in the mountains around Kalavryta. His family held it until it was lost to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> in the later 13th century.</p></div>
